Package: sandtablR
Title: Mass-Casualty Incident Simulation and Machine Learning Workbench
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Raban", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@charite.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742")),
    person("Gerhard", "Achatz", role = "aut"))
Description: A generic framework for mass-casualty incident tabletop exercise
    simulation, decision-path analysis, and machine learning. Provides a
    discrete-event patient-flow engine, a tidy data model for scenarios,
    patient cards and decision paths, synthetic cohort generation, supervised
    triage and therapy-concept classification spanning interpretable and
    black-box models, sequence analysis of participant decision paths, and a
    model-agnostic explainability layer. An interactive 'shiny' workbench ties
    the pieces together for scenario building, simulation, model training,
    comparison and visualisation.
